{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits","id":1169509,"title":"The Spirit of the Season - Pack Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-21T15:59:23-08:00","id":1169509,"title":"The Spirit of the Season - Pack Merits","content":"Spirits of Giving are feasting on the resonance of the season at the moment, and who am I to try and stop their meal?<br /> <br /> For the next three days I'll be posting 17 new Pack Merits for your enjoyment, discussion, or derision (you Forsaken fans are an ornery lot).<br /> <br /> For context around the material: I wrote these as a fan supplement after The Pack was finalised and working its way through the publication cycle. None of the them were cut from the book, and I wasn't contracted to write any of them. I had intended to have Stew post them as a dev blog at some point, but we've been without a developer for some time, so I'm sharing them for people to use or not as they like. While none of these merits are 'official', they're all written in the spirit of The Pack, with that book's balance and needs in mind. It's up to your group how much you do or don't want to use them.<br /> <br /> The first two focus on <i>Kuruth</i>. The books aren't 100% clear on whether <i>Basu-Im</i> werewolves are only immune to the rages of others in their pack, or all werewolves in the death rage. Here's one merit each for whichever way you want it to work.<br /> <br /> <hr /><b><i>Kuruth</i> \u2014 Linked Rage (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> When warring packs descend into <i>Kuruth</i> to continue the fight the result is often devastating for both packs. No one is safe from the blood-drenched frenzy of violence, including nearby Wolf-Blooded and humans of either pack. With this Merit, the pack may choose to conceal itself from the enemy\u2019s rage.<br /> Any of the pack\u2019s Uratha who are in <i>Basu-Im</i> are ignored as targets by the rival pack\u2019s frenzying werewolves, just as if they were also members of that pack. The characters essentially become part of their rival pack and will fight alongside them as long as <i>Kuruth</i> endures. No one else is safe from the characters, and packmates not in <i>Basu-Im</i> are acceptable targets. As part of this Merit, <i>Uratha</i> may allow the fire of their opponent\u2019s frenzy kindle their Rage as well. Upon sensing a member of the other pack fall into <i>Basu-Im</i>, the character may link her Rage and enter <i>Basu-Im</i> as if the other werewolf were a member of her own pack.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The characters concealing themselves within Rage cannot later choose to attack their adoptive pack while they\u2019re still in <i>Kuruth</i>. Once linked, the immunity and shared hatred lasts until both packs naturally exhaust their Rage. This may result in characters coming to their senses deep within enemy territory. <br /> <br /> <hr /><b><i>Kuruth</i> \u2014 Us Against Them (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Despite the best planning and tactical deployment, fights between packs often descend into the whirling death-frenzy of <i>Kuruth</i>. When the <i>Basu-Im</i> takes hold, the Uratha of both packs inevitably break off their animosity towards each other and destroy everything else around them. Packs with this Merit can still discern friend from foe even within the throes of <i>Kuruth</i>. Werewolves of the pack with this Merit may choose to attack (non-pack) Uratha also in <i>Basu-Im</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Attacking those who believe themselves your allies removes the pack\u2019s immunity from hostility. The turn after any <i>Basu-Im</i> suffering member of the pack attacks a rival in <i>Basu-Im</i>, the rival\u2019s pack also gains the ability to identify the attacking pack as the enemy. The violence and bloodshed displayed in such <i>Kuruth</i>-fueled pack-against-pack is truly terrifying to witness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:11:28-08:00","id":1169528,"title":"","content":"Next, I'll post Merits that look at how packmates draw strength from each other. <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Bone, Blood, and Belonging (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> A character\u2019s Anchors reaffirm her sense of identity and provide inner strength by confirming who she believes herself to be. Within the pack, disparate personalities come together to make something bigger than individuals. As individuals strengthen their inner resolve, the pack gains strength. When a packmate gains Willpower \u2014 whether it comes from Blood, Bone, Virtue or Vice \u2014 other members of the pack may also regain a point of Willpower if they can see or otherwise directly sense their packmate\u2019s renewed sense of purpose. A character may only benefit from this once per session, and she may only gain a single point of Willpower regardless of how many her packmate regained. <hr /><br /> <b>Extended Effort (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Though every pack knows how to work together, packs with this merit have refined cooperation to an art form. Packmates can wring the last drop of effort from each other, pushing their fellows beyond limits of endurance and despite diminishing returns. When working towards a teamwork extended action, secondary actors may forgo their dice roll to give the primary actor one additional roll beyond her limit. Though her chances of success drop off as packmates exhaust themselves, the additional time may be all she requires for success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 12-21-2017, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:16:19-08:00","id":1169529,"title":"","content":"(I tried editing this one into the previous post, but it doesn't seem to be working. Apologies if it appears twice.)<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Extended Effort (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Though every pack knows how to work together, packs with this merit have refined cooperation to an art form. Packmates can wring the last drop of effort from each other, pushing their fellows beyond limits of endurance and despite diminishing returns. When working towards a teamwork extended action, secondary actors may forgo their dice roll to give the primary actor one additional roll beyond her limit. Though her chances of success drop off as packmates exhaust themselves, the additional time may be all she requires for success.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:59:04-08:00","id":1169542,"title":"","content":"And lastly for today, something for the Pack to draw on its extended membership.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Crowd Support (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Too many werewolves overlook the utility of the broader pack. They focus on the Uratha, and perhaps the Wolf-Blooded with useful Tells, but ignore the humans. Not so packs with this Merit, who draw on every member of the pack for support. Once per session, the pack may absolutely depend on packmate support. The pack defines one task that must either be able to be completed within a Scene, or reach a specific milestone. Examples include killing all rivals in a firefight (which could be achieved within the Scene), or brokering a temporary truce to cross a rival pack\u2019s territory while pursuing the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> (which is a milestone for the Sacred Hunt to continue unmolested). As long as members of the extended pack could conceivably assist and are available to do so, players may add three dice to rolls related to that goal until the end of the Scene.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Friends of Friends (\u2022, \u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The pack works to build contacts and allies within and outside its territory, working outwards from the people the pack knows to their \u2018friends-of-friends\u2019 network. Once per session, packmates can tap into their existing social networks to reach out to others with the skills or knowledge needed by the pack. Roll the dots in this merit as a dice pool, adding one die for each character with dots in Allies, Contacts, Mentor, Retainer, or Staff. (Storytellers may decide that other Social Merits are also suitable to be added to this roll.)<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The pack insults the wrong people and everyone suffers massive blows to their reputations. No packmate can use any Human Merit that draws on social connections for the remainder of the session.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The pack can\u2019t find anyone else to help them, nor can any of their friends. The pack may covert Failure to Dramatic Failure and take a Pack Beat.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The pack\u2019s social network finds someone who is willing to help the pack. Divide the number of successes between Allies, Contacts, Retainer or Staff, at one success per dot. No single Merit may be higher than the number of dots the pack has in <i>Friends of Friends</i>, nor can the pack gain more than twice the number of dots they have in this Merit. These additional Social Merits disappear either at the end of the scene in which they are used, or at the end of the session.<br /> The pack (or individual packmates) can spend Pack Experiences on making these people ongoing members of the pack\u2019s existence, at the usual Merit cost.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As per Success, but the pack can build Merits up to twice their dots in <i>Friends of Friends</i>; these Merits linger two sessions if not used, but still expire at the end of the scene in which they are used.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T18:11:58-08:00","id":1169544,"title":"","content":"Nice! Really gives some more mechanical oomph to the extended pack. I especially like Crowd Support and Bone, Blood and Belonging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T19:49:32-08:00","id":1169561,"title":"","content":"I definitely like how they explore those connections in unique ways without being overwhelming. Each one adds twists and turns to things that are already in the game in awesome ways!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T11:25:33-08:00","id":1169687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits#post1169509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Kuruth</i> \u2014 Linked Rage (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> When warring packs descend into <i>Kuruth</i> to continue the fight the result is often devastating for both packs. No one is safe from the blood-drenched frenzy of violence, including nearby Wolf-Blooded and humans of either pack. With this Merit, the pack may choose to conceal itself from the enemy\u2019s rage.<br /> Any of the pack\u2019s Uratha who are in <i>Basu-Im</i> are ignored as targets by the rival pack\u2019s frenzying werewolves, just as if they were also members of that pack. The characters essentially become part of their rival pack and will fight alongside them as long as <i>Kuruth</i> endures. No one else is safe from the characters, and packmates not in <i>Basu-Im</i> are acceptable targets. As part of this Merit, <i>Uratha</i> may allow the fire of their opponent\u2019s frenzy kindle their Rage as well. Upon sensing a member of the other pack fall into <i>Basu-Im</i>, the character may link her Rage and enter <i>Basu-Im</i> as if the other werewolf were a member of her own pack.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The characters concealing themselves within Rage cannot later choose to attack their adoptive pack while they\u2019re still in <i>Kuruth</i>. Once linked, the immunity and shared hatred lasts until both packs naturally exhaust their Rage. This may result in characters coming to their senses deep within enemy territory. <hr /><b><i>Kuruth</i> \u2014 Us Against Them (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Despite the best planning and tactical deployment, fights between packs often descend into the whirling death-frenzy of <i>Kuruth</i>. When the <i>Basu-Im</i> takes hold, the Uratha of both packs inevitably break off their animosity towards each other and destroy everything else around them. Packs with this Merit can still discern friend from foe even within the throes of <i>Kuruth</i>. Werewolves of the pack with this Merit may choose to attack (non-pack) Uratha also in <i>Basu-Im</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Attacking those who believe themselves your allies removes the pack\u2019s immunity from hostility. The turn after any <i>Basu-Im</i> suffering member of the pack attacks a rival in <i>Basu-Im</i>, the rival\u2019s pack also gains the ability to identify the attacking pack as the enemy. The violence and bloodshed displayed in such <i>Kuruth</i>-fueled pack-against-pack is truly terrifying to witness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's my English as Second Language - but I cannot understand difference between those mechanics. Could you shown, I don't know, maybe on examples working of those Merits? Let's assume we have Pack A and B - and one Uratha in Pack A start to go <i>Basu-Im</i> - so what happens on those scenarios?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-22-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T12:43:25-08:00","id":1169707,"title":"","content":"Also, if I remember correctly from <b>The Pack</b> book, Pack Merits works that each member is assumed to have it when Pack - as general - buy those Merits, yes? So any member of Pack can activate any 'power' the Pack is having on to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T17:53:13-08:00","id":1169787,"title":"","content":"What do I have for you today? Five Pack Merits, so we can round out the 17 with six tomorrow.<br /> <br /> First, a couple of merits for the ritemasters out there.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Combined Rites (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Most rites occur in isolation as the magic of the spirit world rejects combination. Something about packs with this Merit overcomes this limitation.<br /> When performing rites, the pack may attempt multiple rites at once \u2014 this can include multiple performances of the same rite, resulting in several iterations of the rite\u2019s effect. Every rite must have a separate ritemaster who builds successes towards her required total. Secondary performers must follow the dice pools of one of the rites being performed, but their successes enhance the dice pools of all ritemasters.<br /> <br /> Combining rites in this manner isn\u2019t simple. The successes required to perform each rite increase by 5 per additional rite. Similarly, the available time doesn\u2019t increase \u2014 the ritemaster with the lowest Attribute + Skill + Specialty total determines the group\u2019s maximum number of rolls. Finally, performers of rites requiring fewer successes than others can\u2019t simply stop when that rite has sufficient successes. The ritemaster for that rite becomes another secondary performer for the other ritemasters.<br /> <br /> When the rite requiring the greatest number of successes achieves its goal, the effect of each rite triggers. If any individual rite fails to reach its target \u2014 regardless of whether other rites have successfully reached their goals \u2014 all rites fail and every ritemaster suffers the Shadowlash Condition.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Fast Rites (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Through raw talent, practice, or some supernatural blessing, your pack performs rites more quickly than others. The symbolism falls into place and the energies coalesce in ways that make other packs jealous. The ritemaster subtracts one from the target number of successes for each dot the pack has in this Merit, to a minimum of one. Creatures opposing the rite in a contested roll gain the same benefit as the pack, reducing their target successes by the same amount.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Performing rites can be flexible, but the magic is unforgiving. If the ritemaster fails to achieve any successes on a roll, the rite falls apart and she suffers the effects of a Dramatic Failure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T20:26:05-08:00","id":1169812,"title":"","content":"Part two - something for the furry spirit cops.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Court Familiarity (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Territory extends both sides of the Gauntlet, and the pack must understand the threats and opportunities in both the <i>Hisil</i> and the physical world. With this Merit, the pack knows the spirit denizens well. Either through painstaking effort or instinctive understanding, the pack understands the spiritual hierarchy and the factional politics within. Members of the pack gain a 2 dice bonus to rolls interacting with spirits of their territory \u2014 this doesn\u2019t apply to combat rolls \u2014 and improve Social maneuvering first impressions one step when dealing with spirits that consider the territory home.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Totem Court (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Most totems leave behind their place in the Shadow when they take on a pack bond. Your pack\u2019s totem has maintained its position and rules a court of lesser spirits. The dot rating represents both the number of <i>umia</i> or <i>ilthum</i> the totem has influence over, but also the degree to which its commands are obeyed. The players and Storyteller should work together to broadly define the spirit groups in the court, but they should either consist of <i>umia</i> similar to the totem, or <i>ilthum</i> inhabiting the territory\u2019s <i>Hisil</i>. No spirit servant can be of higher Rank than the totem, and no more than one group should be of equivalent Rank, unless the totem is itself Rank 1.<br /> At one dot the totem can expect small favors or the use of simple Influence. At three dots the spirits will engage in riskier behavior for their ruler, while at five dots the spirits will risk their existence if so commanded.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Nothing is ever free in spirit hierarchies. Everything must be paid for, and even a court ruler pays its servants in protection, favors, or access to essence. In each lunar month, the totem must devote one day per dot tending to its court. The pack may be present for this, but if they have other business, the totem cannot join them until the next day. Additionally, the totem will ask for the pack\u2019s assistance in providing its payment to the court. If the court provides services for the pack, the totem will expect them to pay in kind or risk its displeasure.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T21:03:14-08:00","id":1169819,"title":"","content":"Last one for today... the season encourages us to reflect on how important pack is.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Pack is All (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The pack provides assistance in the hunt, companionship along a difficult existence, and protection against foes who would seek to make Uratha their prey. Some packs even go beyond this and serve as an anchor for the Uratha soul; helping to balance the werewolf nature against itself. Packs with this Merit have an additional Touchstone (<b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> p. 87) that always tries to keep them from losing the balance. Once per session, each packmate may gain +2 to resist Harmony changes that would move them further from Harmony 5, as long as the Breaking Point occurred in service to the pack. For non-Uratha, this benefit may be applied to resist any breaking point in service to the pack, but only once per session.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T21:18:01-08:00","id":1169821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1169687#post1169687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's my English as Second Language - but I cannot understand difference between those mechanics. Could you shown, I don't know, maybe on examples working of those Merits? Let's assume we have Pack A and B - and one Uratha in Pack A start to go <i>Basu-Im</i> - so what happens on those scenarios?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the core book. 'When in Basu-Im, a werewolf suffers rage as though in Gauru, but everyone is a victim except other werewolves in Basu-Im.' What this can imply is that if Werewolf A and Werewolf B are fighting, and Werewolf A goes into Basu-Im, if Werewolf B goes into Basu-Im too, they will stop fighting each other and instead attack something else that isn't in Basu-Im.<br /> <br /> Since <i><b>among packs</b></i>, Basu-Im is sort of contagious, this can mean that werewolf-on-werewolf battles can be ended by someone on both sides going into Basu-Im. As more werewolves go into Basu-Im, you have less targets, until you have a horde of raging werewolves attacking anything but each other.<br /> <br /> With Linked Rage.<br /> 1. The Contagion (where you sense a packmate in Basu-Im and fall into Basu-Im) can stretch beyond packs. So if an enemy goes Basu-Im, you can go Basu-Im in return, ending the conflict between you two.<br /> 2. You can't decide to go and attack them once you've joined them, at least while you're still raging. You basically become a single, raging mob.<br /> <br /> With Us Against Them.<br /> 1. When in Basu-Im, you can still attack non-packmembers in Basu-Im.<br /> 2. Enemies in Basu-Im, if attacked, will consider you an applicable opponent. So if you go into Basu-Im, you can't just attack them and have them not attack you just because they don't have the Merit.<br /> <br /> It's nice ways to work with the system, I think.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> These totem merits are really nice, even as someone who doesn't play spirit cop, I do like having a totem who isn't 'on the outs' with the locals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T23:01:01-08:00","id":1169834,"title":"","content":"The \u2018spirit cop\u2019 thing was a joke towards 1st edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Glad you like them. More to come tomorrow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T17:01:29-08:00","id":1170046,"title":"","content":"Christmas Eve, and what do we have for you today? How about something for your territory?<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Eyes Everywhere (\u2022\u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Within the pack\u2019s territory, even the people and spirits not bound to the pack know to keep their eyes open, and who to tell when they notice something strange. At three dots, intruders to the territory must succeed on a Wits + Stealth or Streetwise (depending on rural or urban territory) roll when they enter or something notices them and warns the pack. This doesn\u2019t apply to intruders using supernatural powers to hide their presence. At four dots, all mundane attempts at concealment or blending with the population suffer a three-dice penalty. At five dots, the dice penalty and test when entering the territory also apply to creatures concealed by supernatural means. This Merit works on both sides of the Gauntlet \u2014 intruders in the <i>Hisil</i> are just as likely to be detected.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Territory Feature (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>The territory has a location that is specifically useful to pack. A library with helpful staff may be invaluable when the pack researches its prey. A clinic where the doctors look the other way in return for protection may keep the non-Uratha members healthy after a fight. A trendy bar where assistants to the rich and powerful congregate could provide introductions and favors for the pack.<br /> <br /> When taking this Merit, the pack defines the location and chooses an associated Skill per dot. Each dot applies to a single Skill, but multiple dots may add to the same Skill. When in the location, pack members may add one die per dot to dice pools involving these Skills.<br /> <br /> This Merit may be taken multiple times, each time representing a different location.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Locations of importance to the pack tend to draw attention. People investigating the pack are more likely to find these locations before others, gaining +1 to relevant dice pools per Territory Feature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:11:36-08:00","id":1170070,"title":"","content":"Is &quot;Territory Feature&quot; basically just a slightly reframed Library or Staff Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:14:30-08:00","id":1170071,"title":"","content":"Part two - what's a pack without a reputation?<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Renown by Association (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The world sees the pack as a unit. The individuals matter less than the whole; the legends attributed of the pack rarely name which packmate performed the deed. With this unity comes strength. Each scene, members of the pack may substitute the Renown rating of another packmate for their own. This substituted rating lasts until the end of the scene. Each character may still only do so once per scene. This Merit is not limited to Uratha. Wolf-Blooded and human members of the pack may also draw on Uratha Renown. This doesn\u2019t grant access to Gifts or other powers, but does allow the non-Uratha borrower to flare Renown (<b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> p. 99) as if it were his own.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The pack faces higher expectations than its peers when raising Renown. The Uratha must overcome greater obstacles and higher stakes to justifying an increase in Renown. The Storyteller decides what is appropriate, but as a guide, the degree of challenge to raise Renown may be one level higher than the actual dot rating the character seeks.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Renowned Pack (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> The pack is well known in Uratha society for the great deeds of its members. Just being part of this pack means other Uratha will know of you (or at least the pack) and will likely give packmates due respect, however grudgingly.<br /> <br /> This Merit can be purchased multiple times, once for each type of Renown. A pack known for its creativity and boldness may have Renowned Pack (Cunning) \u2022\u2022\u2022 and Renowned Pack (Glory) \u2022. Once per session, a member of the pack may apply these dots as bonus dice to social rolls with other packs as long as she engages on topics appropriate to the Renown. She may choose to reduce this bonus to improve her first impression with another pack on a die per level basis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:17:39-08:00","id":1170073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1170070#post1170070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is &quot;Territory Feature&quot; basically just a slightly reframed Library or Staff Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. If you choose to see it that way that's fine, but it's a different effect and applicability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 12-23-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:35:14-08:00","id":1170075,"title":"","content":"Second last, once again calling on the pack to assist the hunt.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Hunting Party (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Though Uratha are superb trackers, the Wolf-Blooded and human packmates add to the effort by expanding the search area and reporting fresh tracks and leads to follow. This merit can be purchased up to two times, once each for Urban and Rural. Subtract dots in Hunting Party (Urban) from the prey\u2019s Streetwise when determining how well the prey evades tracking. Similarly, subtract dots of Hunting Party (Rural) from the prey\u2019s Survival. This Merit works with both Uncontested and Contested tracking maneuvers. This Merit can only be used if a reasonable number of the extended pack is available to assist with the hunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:40:40-08:00","id":1170076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1170070#post1170070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is &quot;Territory Feature&quot; basically just a slightly reframed Library or Staff Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Add your dots as a bonus to extended rolls with one Mental Skill&quot; and &quot;Get one automatic success on one Skill per dot&quot; don't really compare to &quot;Distribute your dots among up to as many Skills as bonus dice on all rolls with those Skills.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> To double-check: Is the +1 in the Drawback per dot in Territory Feature or per separate instance of Territory Feature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T21:07:23-08:00","id":1170081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1170076#post1170076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Add your dots as a bonus to extended rolls with one Mental Skill&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Get one automatic success on one Skill per dot&amp;quot; don't really compare to &amp;quot;Distribute your dots among up to as many Skills as bonus dice on all rolls with those Skills.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> To double-check: Is the +1 in the Drawback per dot in Territory Feature or per separate instance of Territory Feature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. It\u2019s +1 per Territory feature, regardless of its level. Having a 3-dot Public Library would be +1 to people investigating the pack\u2019s territory, whereas having a 3-dot Library, 1-dot Mechanic Workshop and 2-dot Shooting Range would give +3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T21:57:40-08:00","id":1170089,"title":"","content":"And lucky last, a nice long one to round them off, and something to define the pack's place in the mundane world. This one was based on, or inspired by, some other merit. I think it was the profession merit, but expanded out for a group rather than an individual. I could be wrong, it has been a couple of years.<br /> <br /> (This one comes complete with formatting tags as well!)<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Professional Pack (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Many packs present a face to the human word that raises expectations of behavior. Human authorities expect gang-like packs to be violent and involved in criminal dealings. A pack that appears as a religious group would be expected to speak on the spiritual teachings of the group, and proselytize in the community for new converts to the faith. Packs with this Merit are more skilled at understanding the role they play, and presenting themselves accordingly when needed.<br /> <br /> When choosing this Merit, give the pack a Pack Profession fitting the pack\u2019s role (see <b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>sidebar, p. 47 for inspiration). The Merit\u2019s dot rating determines the advantage.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">[sidebar]<br /> <b>Related Organizations</b><br /> When the Professional Pack Merit discusses related organizations, it refers to those other businesses, agencies \u2014 or packs \u2014 who know of the pack\u2019s reputation by having overlapping business interests. At one dot, a gang-like pack most closely resembles a street gang, and may only be known by the rivals who border its territory. At two dots, the gang may also be known by local police and some larger organized crime elements in the city. At five dots, almost everyone knows of the pack. Even though it may still appear as a street gang, federal law enforcement, major crime families, and any firm that wants to conduct business in the territory knows its name and recognizes the power behind it.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, for each dot of this Merit, the Storyteller should allow one \u2018hop\u2019 outside associated circles to decide if another group is a related organization.<br /> [end sidebar]</div> <br /> \u2022 Take My Call: Whether having access to an official phonebook listing, or just asking around the pack, a packmate can make contact with someone to speak with in a related organization. This person has the right reach into that organization for the pack to achieve what it wants, but the individual may be unreceptive or hostile to the character\u2019s approach.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 Reputed: The pack is known within its chosen profession. When dealing with representatives of a related organization packmates may improve Social maneuvering first impressions one step. Even normally hostile groups will begrudgingly allow the pack a chance to speak.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Respected: The pack is well-established and well-known within its profession. When engaging in Social maneuvering with members of a related organization, packmates need to open one less Door than normally required.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Calling in Favors: The pack may draw on the assistance and resources of a related organization. Once per session, a member of the pack may use a three-dot (or less) Merit that the related organization could conceivably have access to. The character doesn\u2019t gain the Merit herself \u2014 the other agency may need to send someone with the Merit to assist the pack. The Storyteller has final say over whether a given Merit is suitable to be subject to use. Calling in favors this way usually requires reciprocation. The related organization is entitled to seek a favor of comparable difficulty from the pack. If the pack refuses, it may not use Professional Pack against that organization until it makes restitution for the offence. This doesn\u2019t apply to favors the pack is incapable of fulfilling \u2014 such requests automatically fail without offence, and the group may ask again until the ledger is balanced.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Hostile Action: The pack is a powerhouse of its chosen industry. Nearly everyone has heard of, and defers to, the pack. Once per chapter, the pack may use its influence to force its will upon a related organization. Choose which packmate will be the primary actor in delivering the demand. (The pack can use teamwork for this roll.) Roll the primary actor\u2019s Presence + Politics, Intimidation, Persuasion or Subterfuge (depending how she approaches the \u2018request\u2019) \u2013 the Resistance of the organization to the demand (see nearby table).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Organizational Damage</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Resistance </b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Recovery Time</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Resistance</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">None or minimal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Less than 24 hours</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Minor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Days</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Moderate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Weeks</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Major</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Months</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Catastrophic</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Years, if at all</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The pack\u2019s demand is forcefully rejected, damaging the pack\u2019s reputation. The pack can\u2019t access the fifth dot of the Professional Pack Merit for the remainder of the story.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The pack\u2019s demand is denied. The pack can\u2019t use any aspect of this Merit on the target organization for the rest of the chapter.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The target performs whatever task the pack demanded, within the limits of what the organization can accomplish. The relationship is diminished and the pack can\u2019t attempt a Hostile Action on the related organization again until the next story. The pack can attempt a Hostile Action against another target in the next chapter.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The target performs the task within the limits of its abilities, and understands that the pack still holds power in the relationship. The pack may target the organization with another Hostile Action in the next chapter, if it wishes to do so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T22:31:43-08:00","id":1170094,"title":"","content":"There you go, everyone. 3400 words to flesh out how your packs interact with the world. Happy Wolfmas, or whatever you\u2019re celebrating.<br /> <br /> All that\u2019s left now is to ask what haven\u2019t I covered yet? Is there anything that a pack needs to do, be seen to do, interact with, or use, that we haven\u2019t covered yet? If so, shout out what we need and I\u2019ll see about extending the seasonal giving through to New Year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T23:23:37-08:00","id":1170102,"title":"","content":"I like Territory Feature, kind of reminds me of the Territories book but far more succinct. I'm sure there's something I'd want about the pack and their spiritual presence but nothing I could put into words off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Professional Pack is really cool, totally seems like it should have been in the Pack book, especially given the examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T23:59:36-08:00","id":1170105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1170102#post1170102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Professional Pack is really cool, totally seems like it should have been in the Pack book, especially given the examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan to give Professional Pack ( Vikings ) to my players from year 800 A.D. game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T00:02:15-08:00","id":1170107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1170081#post1170081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s +1 per Territory feature, regardless of its level. Having a 3-dot Public Library would be +1 to people investigating the pack\u2019s territory, whereas having a 3-dot Library, 1-dot Mechanic Workshop and 2-dot Shooting Range would give +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as I understand, you can have Territory Feature (Bar - Socialize ) 1-dot, Territory Feature (Bar - Persuasion ) 2-dot and Territory Feature (Bar - Streetwise ) 3-dot - all 3 separate Merits connected to the same Bar location? And those would give in sum +3 to investigating pack's territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T00:06:56-08:00","id":1170108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169509-the-spirit-of-the-season-pack-merits?p=1170105#post1170105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--bl